<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Privacy Sandbox Ad Services config for the whole app.

    Exists to resolve a manifest-merger conflict: play-services-measurement-api
    (pulled in by firebase-analytics) and play-services-ads-lite each declare
    the android.adservices.AD_SERVICES_CONFIG property pointing at their own
    resource — ga_ad_services_config.xml and gma_ad_services_config.xml — and
    the merger cannot pick between two different values.

    This is the union of both, which is just the ads one: analytics asks only
    for Attribution, ads asks for Attribution + Topics. Declaring our own file
    and overriding with tools:replace (see AndroidManifest) rather than
    pointing at either library's resource, because those names are the SDKs'
    internals and can change under us on a version bump.
-->
<ad-services-config>
    <!-- Attribution API — required by both Analytics and Ads. -->
    <attribution allowAllToAccess="true" />

    <!-- Topics API — Ads only. -->
    <topics allowAllToAccess="true" />
</ad-services-config>
